# Canonical URL cleanup: force the .html file paths to the clean paths
# used in the sitemap and all internal links, so Google indexes one URL
# per page instead of two. Query strings (e.g. /category.html?cat=X) are
# passed through automatically by Netlify.
/index.html            /                 301!
/new.html               /new             301!
/ai-prompts.html        /ai-prompts      301!
/category.html          /category        301!
/submit.html            /submit          301!
/contact.html           /contact         301!
/privacy-policy.html    /privacy-policy  301!

# Each category now has its own dedicated static page (see the
# category-*.html files) instead of one shared category.html keyed off
# a ?cat= query string, so Google can index 15 distinct pages instead of
# folding them all into one. These are rewrites (200), not redirects, so
# the clean /category/<slug> URL stays in the address bar.
/category/ai-tools                 /category-ai-tools.html                 200
/category/design-inspiration       /category-design-inspiration.html       200
